    "done_when": "Lead ruling 2026-10-02: root-cause the centroid-constrained solve before any resolution ladder; no fix in this node. CPU in place with JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu, on main. (1) Apply the production forward map, as benchmarks/centroid_constrained_fixture_receipt.py builds it for the weak-rotation-reactor-static -110 row at 135 cells, to the analytic Solovev flux of that row, and persist the per-cell residual of the fixed-point map as a receipt and a line-contour residual panel with the wall; a faithful map leaves a residual at discretisation level, so report its sup and its spatial pattern, and cite any S21 map-fidelity measurement of the same fixture. (2) Drive the compensator's flux response through the code path the solve uses (BoundedExteriorFieldUnknown.flux_delta and the prescribed exterior field it reads) with a unit uniform vertical field and a unit uniform radial field, and compare each against its closed form in nova's convention (vertical field: psi proportional to B_z R^2 / 2, with the factor of 2 pi if nova's psi is total flux; radial field: the matching closed form), reporting sign, scale factor and any spatial deviation, with a receipt and panels. (3) Recompute the field the discrete baseline would need to cancel the -6.13e-3 m centroid offset from the measured unit leverage, and compare its sign and size with the converged -2.1256e-2 T. Receipts and panels go under docs/figures/centroid-constrained-oracle-solve/root-cause/closed-forms/; the report at /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/nova/s22/cco-root-cause-map-and-compensator-closed-forms.md states plainly which, if any, is wrong, with the number that shows it.",
